From: OmacVM
Subject: [PATCH] ui: the guest's Caps Lock from its LEDs, tested without AppKit

What: a header with no AppKit in it: whether one Caps Lock press goes to the
guest for an input event, from the Mac's Caps Lock flag, Shift as the guest
has it, and what the guest keyboard's LEDs reported. A Caps Lock LED change
is the answer to a press of ours (one per press, within 500 ms) or the
guest's own lock; a Num Lock or Scroll Lock change is ignored; a report with
no LED changed is the guest's keyboard starting (presses before it went
nowhere), and the guest's lock is what the LED says. A lock gone in the guest
(a new session, a restart inside the VM, a press lost while the guest
started) with the Mac's on is put back at the next event; a lock set in the
guest stays until the Mac's flag changes; a press sent with Shift held that
gets no answer (Omarchy 4.5's Shift + Caps Lock = Compose) leaves the guest's
lock as it is until the Mac's flag changes. Used by
omacvm-cocoa-caps-lock.patch (which explains the why).

Why its own file: so the rules are tested without QEMU or a window
(app/runtime/Tests/keys/test-caps-lock.sh applies this patch to an empty
folder; at build time and in CI).

Upstream: upstreamable together with omacvm-cocoa-caps-lock.patch.
Test: app/runtime/Tests/keys/test-caps-lock.c.

diff --git a/ui/omacvm-capslock.h b/ui/omacvm-capslock.h
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/ui/omacvm-capslock.h
@@ -0,0 +1,138 @@
+/*
+ * OmacVM: the guest's Caps Lock follows the Mac's (#784).
+ *
+ * No AppKit in here, so it is tested on its own
+ * (app/runtime/Tests/keys/test-caps-lock.c); ui/cocoa.m feeds it.
+ *
+ * Caps Lock is a lock in the guest: each press flips it. QEMU sent a press
+ * whenever the Mac's Caps Lock flag differed from what its own presses had
+ * left. The guest can lose its lock without a press from QEMU: a new desktop
+ * session, a restart inside the VM (QEMU keeps running), a press that came
+ * while the guest was still starting. From then on the two were the other way
+ * round until Caps Lock was pressed outside the VM.
+ *
+ * The guest shows its lock on the keyboard's Caps Lock LED (virtio-input's
+ * EV_LED, QEMU's LED notifier with the keyboard's LED mask). The guest
+ * reports only LED changes. What the notifier can bring:
+ * - the Caps Lock LED changed: the answer to a press of ours (one per press,
+ *   within OMACVM_CAPS_SETTLE_MS), or else the guest's own lock;
+ * - only Num Lock or Scroll Lock changed: nothing about Caps Lock;
+ * - no LED changed: the guest's keyboard started (DRIVER_OK,
+ *   omacvm-virtio-input-leds-reset.patch). A press of ours before that went
+ *   nowhere (virtio-input drops events while the driver is not up): the
+ *   guest's lock is what the LED says.
+ * With the guest's own lock known:
+ * - gone (the LED off) while the Mac's is on: one press at the next input
+ *   event puts it back;
+ * - set in the guest (the LED on, by another keyboard): kept until the Mac's
+ *   flag changes, as before.
+ * A guest whose Caps Lock key does not lock (Compose, Escape, Control) never
+ * answers with its LED: one press per change of the Mac's flag, as before.
+ * Shift + Caps Lock may be another key in the guest (Omarchy 4.5's default
+ * omarchy:shift_caps_compose: Compose), while the Mac's flag flips: a press
+ * that went with Shift held and got no answer leaves the guest's lock as its
+ * LED says, until the Mac's flag changes. The Mac's light is then not
+ * applied, never the other way round.
+ *
+ * Limits:
+ * - qemu_input_get_leds_mask(dcl.con) reads the first keyboard handler:
+ *   OmacVM gives QEMU exactly one keyboard (virtio-keyboard-pci, Runner.swift;
+ *   test-caps-lock.sh checks it).
+ * - A guest that drives its Caps Lock LED for something else (xkb's
+ *   grp_led:caps, an LED daemon), or copies another keyboard's lock onto it
+ *   (a USB keyboard passed through), shows a lock that is not its Caps Lock:
+ *   taken as the guest's own (kept), so Caps Lock can be out of step there,
+ *   one press per forced change at most.
+ *
+ * SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-or-later
+ */
+#ifndef OMACVM_CAPSLOCK_H
+#define OMACVM_CAPSLOCK_H
+
+#include <stdbool.h>
+#include <stdint.h>
+
+/* How long the guest's LED may take to answer a press of ours. */
+#define OMACVM_CAPS_SETTLE_MS 500
+
+/* The Caps Lock bit of the LED mask (QEMU_CAPS_LOCK_LED; cocoa.m checks it). */
+#define OMACVM_CAPS_LED (1u << 2)
+
+typedef struct {
+    bool sent;          /* the guest's lock, as far as we know */
+    bool led;           /* the guest's Caps Lock LED, as last reported */
+    bool mac;           /* the Mac's flag as last seen */
+    bool keep;          /* the guest's own: no press until the Mac's flag changes */
+    bool shift;         /* Shift was held in the guest for the last press */
+    uint32_t leds;      /* the guest keyboard's LED mask, as last reported */
+    int inflight;       /* presses of ours whose LED change has not come yet */
+    int64_t press_ms;   /* when the last one went out */
+} OmacVMCaps;
+
+/* Presses with no answer in time: they went nowhere or did not lock. */
+static inline void omacvm_caps_expire(OmacVMCaps *s, int64_t now_ms)
+{
+    if (s->inflight > 0 && now_ms - s->press_ms >= OMACVM_CAPS_SETTLE_MS) {
+        s->inflight = 0;
+        if (s->shift) {
+            /* Shift + Caps Lock was another key (Compose): the lock did not move. */
+            s->sent = s->led;
+            s->keep = true;
+        }
+    }
+}
+
+/* The first input event: the LEDs as they are now (the notifier is added then). */
+static inline void omacvm_caps_start(OmacVMCaps *s, uint32_t leds)
+{
+    s->leds = leds;
+    s->led = s->sent = s->keep = (leds & OMACVM_CAPS_LED) != 0;
+}
+
+/* QEMU's LED notifier: leds is the guest keyboard's LED mask now. */
+static inline void omacvm_caps_leds(OmacVMCaps *s, uint32_t leds, int64_t now_ms)
+{
+    bool led = (leds & OMACVM_CAPS_LED) != 0;
+
+    omacvm_caps_expire(s, now_ms);
+    if (leds == s->leds) {
+        /* No LED changed: the guest's keyboard started; our presses went nowhere. */
+        s->inflight = 0;
+    } else {
+        s->leds = leds;
+        if (led == s->led) {
+            return;     /* Num Lock or Scroll Lock */
+        }
+        s->led = led;
+        if (s->inflight > 0) {
+            s->inflight--;
+            return;     /* the answer to a press of ours */
+        }
+    }
+    /* The guest's own lock: a new session or a restart (off), another keyboard (on). */
+    s->sent = led;
+    s->keep = led;
+}
+
+/*
+ * One input event: true when one Caps Lock press (down, up) goes to the guest
+ * now. mac: the Mac's Caps Lock flag; shift: Shift is held in the guest.
+ */
+static inline bool omacvm_caps_step(OmacVMCaps *s, bool mac, bool shift, int64_t now_ms)
+{
+    omacvm_caps_expire(s, now_ms);
+    if (mac != s->mac) {
+        s->mac = mac;
+        s->keep = false;
+    }
+    if (mac == s->sent || s->keep) {
+        return false;
+    }
+    s->sent = mac;
+    s->shift = shift;
+    s->inflight++;
+    s->press_ms = now_ms;
+    return true;
+}
+
+#endif
